<title>ITALY: SP Brescia confirms interest in Bergamasco.</title>
<headline>SP Brescia confirms interest in Bergamasco.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian banking group San Paolo di Brescia on Tuesday confirmed its interest in purchasing fellow banking group Credito Bergamasco, which is controlled by French banking group Credit Lyonnais.</p>
<p>A San Paolo di Brescia statement said that the bank had presented to Merrill Lynch International a preliminary non-binding offer of interest for the acquisition of Credito Bergamasco. Merrill Lynch is acting as adviser to the French bank for the sale of the Bergamo-based bank in northern Italy.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
